rpresser wrote:
> A google search reveals that saddlebags have been YANI'd many times,
> starting in 1998, but we still don't have them. Would they be too
> useful, and hence unbalancing?

I've considered implementing it from time to time, but never come up
with a decent interface for it. The commands that are traditionally
used for interacting with containers, (a)pply and # loot, have other
uses when it comes to saddles.

I suppose you could add an additional question to the # loot sequence:

# loot
Loot in what direction? h
Do you want to remove the saddle from the horse? [yn] n
Do you want to loot the saddlebags? [yn] y

This second question is kind of redundant. If you answer no, there will
be nothing else you can do (you can't loot a container from a
neighbouring cell, nor while your steed is standing on it). So it could
go straight into "You loot the horse's saddle bags...".

Applying a saddle could be trickier. Usually it goes straight into "In
what direction?". It would be annoying to have a "Do you want to loot
the saddle-bags?" question first.

